nodecode-secretshield is a rewrite of Whydiriki700's Whydiriki700/secretshield:

  https://github.com/Whydiriki700/secretshield
  commit d3561130502cf8f773c01574bef79d870cf5a52d
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Riki Wahyudi (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the detector table (vendor credential formats plus one assignment
context), the masked preview, the four modes (enforce, redact, warn, off) and
the `disabled_kinds` setting, the metadata-only incident ledger, and the two
user surfaces (`/secretshield` and the `shield_status` tool, from the
original's `/shield` and `shield_status`). Hermes's hooks are Nodecode's hook
chain on its single `:TOOL` point: the pre-call phase stops or rewrites the
arguments, the post-call phase records what a tool printed. The original's
first-turn note is one `:ROUND` hook.

Left out: the finished-reply rewrite (`transform_llm_output`). Nodecode streams
a reply as it is written, and there is no point at which a finished reply can
be rewritten without holding the stream, so a credential quoted in a reply is
caught on its way back out as a tool call, or by `/secretshield <text>`.
Also left out: the `hermes secretshield` subcommand (a Nodecode cell has one
command and one tool), and the plugin's own test file, whose cases are
rewritten here.
